error[Z0410]: `dist.negbinomial` takes `p:` or `mu:`, not both
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:39
  |
1 | dist.negbinomial(size: 3, p: 0.4, mu: 2)
  |                                       ^ a second parameterisation
  |
  = help: `size:` with `p:` counts failures before the size-th success; `mu:` with `size:` is the mean parameterisation (NB2)

error[Z0406]: `dist.negbinomial` needs `p:` or `mu:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:6
  |
1 | dist.negbinomial(size: 3)
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^ neither is given
  |
  = help: `dist.negbinomial(size: 3, p: 0.4)` or `dist.negbinomial(mu: 4.5, size: 3)`

error[Z0413]: `p` of `dist.negbinomial` must be a probability above 0 and at most 1, but this is 0
