  |                              ^ outside the parameter's domain
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.negbinomial` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0413]: `upper` of `dist.truncated` must exceed `lower`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:48
  |
1 | dist.truncated(dist.normal(), lower: 2, upper: 1)
  |                                                ^ not above `lower`
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.truncated` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0413]: the interval of `dist.truncated` holds no probability of the distribution
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:6
  |
1 | dist.truncated(dist.uniform(), lower: 5, upper: 6)
  |      ^^^^^^^^^ an empty truncation
  |
  = help: choose bounds inside the distribution's support, where its probability is not zero

warning: sqrt of a negative number gave NA (line 1)
  = help: a negative number has no real square root; `where(x >= 0)` keeps the rows that have one
error[Z0413]: `lower` of `dist.truncated` must be a number, but this is NA
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:38
  |
1 | dist.truncated(dist.normal(), lower: sqrt(-1))
  |                                      ^^^^^^^^ outside the parameter's domain

error[Z0401]: `probs` of `dist.mixture` must hold one probability per distribution: 1 distributions, 2 probabilities
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:38
  |
1 | dist.mixture([dist.normal()], probs: [0.3, 0.7])
  |                                      ^^^^^^^^^^ the wrong number of probabilities

error[Z0413]: `probs` of `dist.mixture` must be probabilities of 0 or more that sum to one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:60
  |
1 | dist.mixture([dist.normal(), dist.normal(mean: 3)], probs: [0.3, 0.6])
  |                                                            ^^^^^^^^^^ these sum to 0.9
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.mixture` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0406]: `dist.mixture` needs `probs:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:6
  |
1 | dist.mixture([dist.normal(), dist.normal(mean: 3)])
  |      ^^^^^^^ `probs:` is missing
  |
  = help: one probability per distribution, summing to one: `probs: [0.3, 0.7]`

error[Z0401]: `dist.mixture` needs a list of at least one distribution
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:14
  |
1 | dist.mixture([], probs: [])
  |              ^^ no distributions here
